# Every pattern here is anchored with a leading slash, and that is not tidiness.
#
# `.vercelignore` follows .gitignore matching, where a pattern without a slash
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth. In the harness, an unanchored
# `tools/` also matched `app/tools/` and dropped a route from the deployment
# while every local check passed. There is no `app/tools` here today; anchoring
# means there never can be a day when adding one silently breaks the build.

# The environment is a plain Next.js app. Nothing here launches a browser or
# reaches a model, so there is no Playwright to keep out of the build — that
# moved to the harness with everything else.

# Tests and the mutation tool are for a developer machine and CI.
/tests/
/tools/
